    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0861" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p1/pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower Library, Eisenhower papers, Whitman
                    file</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the President to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-03-31">March 31, 1953</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I did not see the final dispatch sent to Clark on Sunday evening.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d428-f1"/> However, I assume that it contained the statement that
                    the entire process of exchanging sick and wounded was to be a completed fact
                    before broader negotiations could be undertaken.</p>
                <p>I think it important, also, that every responsible official in the Administration
                    who may be called upon to speak a public word on this subject understand this
                    particular point thoroughly.</p>
                <closer><signed>D.D.E.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d428-f1" n="1" xml:id="d428-f1-content">
                <p>The reference was to telegram JCS 935136 to Clark, Mar. 29, <ref target="#pg822"
                        >p. 822</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
